Registration and preservation
------------------------------

register accepts the exact generic aggregate, genuine aggregate execution
and distinct execution review. It constructs12 or fewer new parent records,
1..4 shared strict nodes and one cache bank. Old inline cache values, bank
order, unknown fields, other subjects, measurements and intake completion
stay raw byte spans. Strict/supplier profiles, complete attempt histories,
Original payload digests and explicit cover indices are retained. New
schemas are distinct V2 subjects; downstream collectors must admit these
schemas explicitly before any final level/census claim.

Beforeimages are exact old bytes. Runtime and complete new stage images
are immutable. Only controller/current.json and current_intake.json are
replaced. Their exact canonical paths and fresh stage paths appear together
in Core metadata_cas_targets; both content multiplicities are charged to
the images component. Core write_files still writes only fresh/equal targets.
A separate production CAS function checks both whole old pointers, verifies
both staged bodies, rereads BOTH old pointers immediately before the FIRST
replace, then performs the two fixed replacements and fsync/readback.
Runtime is selected by controller and is not a third overwritten target.
Root must maintain a sole-writer window; multi-file atomicity is not claimed.
A failure during replacement leaves the complete immutable before/after
images for an explicitly authorized recovery. It gives no successful
registration or permission to start another cohort.

check_registration authenticates the genuine registration, exact live
pointers and staged before/after bodies, every protected raw value, old
cache values, all new parent/shared/attempt/profile/index joins and the
coherent new prefix. A distinct execution/provenance adoption is still
required. There is no whole-manuscript, open-conjecture, Lean, census or
compression-measurement credit from these administrative steps.

Fresh controls and limits of their claim
----------------------------------------

The metadata controls use actual production helpers for full scientific
ROLE mapping under both profiles, bounded closing reads, complete IO
arithmetic, SDK/frame and guard identity/admission structures, empty/explicit
attempt maps, type/profile/scope failures, raw JSON preservation,156-slot
framing, Core's fixed-CAS declarations and the production CAS ordering.
They include wrong/duplicate targets, swapped/reused stages, Boolean maxima,
altered old refs, wrong entry-role admission, missing/double-counted image
rows and late whole-old change before the first replace. The latter uses
explicit in-memory callbacks; it proves production ordering/refusal, not
observed filesystem atomicity or process-kill behavior. No genuine SDK,
Root grant, Original point/forest or successful actual is fabricated by a
fixture. Actual resource/recorder controls and real execution reviews are
separate prerequisites. Every test in this package remains unrun until
independent Source review and Root ownership/authority.
SDK fixtures check structural predicates only; they are never represented
as genuine API facts. Closing-read callbacks prove refusal before reading
a changed extent, not an observed concurrent filesystem race.
